  "@id": "https://pices-data.github.io/odis/records/zenodo-23605387.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Salmonid Stomach Content Examination Aboard the R/V Wakatake maru in the Central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea during the Summer of 2002 (BASIS Japan)",
  "description": "The Wakatake maru (666 gross tons) departed Kushiro on June 8, 2002 and returned on July 21, 2002. There were 28 experimental fishing stations during the cruise. Nineteen fishing stations were located in the vicinity of 180º longitude from 41ºN to 58º30メN latitude, and nine operations were conducted in the international waters of the central Bering Sea. Stomach samples were collected from all species of salmon and steelhead trout. These samples were collected from a maximum of 10 fish per species from longline mortalities and from a variety of research-mesh sizes and from the commercial mesh gillnet (C- and A-gear). These samples were examined while onboard the vessel. The stomach samples were weighed to the nearest gram before and after removal of the contents, and the weight of the stomach contents obtained by subtraction. The stomach contents were examined using a binocular microscope and separated into several prey categories. The percent volume in each prey category was estimated by eye. [Reference: Tanaka, H, N. Davis, T. Onuma, M. Yamada, Y. Yamamoto, and S. Tsuchiya. 2002. International salmon research aboard the R/V Wakatake maru in the central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea during the summer of 2002. (NPAFC Doc. 622). 21 p. Hokkaido National Fisheries Research Institute, Fisheries Research Agency, 116 Katsurakoi, Kushiro 085-0802, Japan.] This report is available at http://www.npafc.org/BASIS/622(Japan).pdf\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.\n\nPurpose: To monitor the stock condition of salmon ( Oncorhynchus spp.) in the central North Pacific Ocean and Bering Sea.",
  "url": "https://zenodo.org/records/23605388",
